mako
====

A lightweight notification daemon for Wayland compositors (tested on
Sway). It implements the FreeDesktop Notifications Specification over
D-Bus, with support for custom match rules, renderers, icons and
animations.

This package also includes makoctl, a command-line tool to control
mako (list, dismiss, pause and resume notifications).

Homepage: https://github.com/emersion/mako

Dependencies
------------

Slackware core (full install): cairo, pango, glib2, gdk-pixbuf2,
wayland (client/cursor), wayland-protocols >= 1.32, scdoc (man pages),
bash-completion (completions).

SBo / other: elogind (provides the sd-bus API; pinned via
-Dsd-bus-provider=libelogind in the SlackBuild).

Build notes
-----------

Built with meson. All feature flags are pinned explicitly for
reproducibility:

  -Dsd-bus-provider=libelogind  libsystemd is not installed; elogind
                                 provides a compatible sd-bus API.
  -Dicons=enabled               gdk-pixbuf-2.0 is core.
  -Dman-pages=enabled           scdoc is core (>= 1.9.7 required).
  -Dbash-completions=true       bash-completion is core; zsh/fish
                                 completions left disabled (not in a
                                 full install).

Running
-------

mako starts on demand via D-Bus activation. For Sway, add
`exec mako` to your config. Configuration lives in mako.config
(see `man mako.5`).
